{"text": "blueprint:\n  name: FLARE\n  description: >\n    FLARE: phase-based circadian lighting - sets brightness/colour\n    temperature from a FLARE schedule sensor,\n    keeping lights updated as it changes, and turns them off a while\n    after occupancy clears. Full details on every input:\n    [the blueprint reference](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/).\n\n\n    Blueprint version 0.0.0-dev - the integration raises a repair when a\n    newer one is available.\n  domain: automation\n  author: Dan Spencer\n  homeassistant:\n    # Required by the occupancy.* triggers/conditions.\n    min_version: 2026.4.0\n  input:\n    schedule:\n      name: Schedule\n      description: >\n        The FLARE schedule the room follows: the brightness and colour\n        temperature it applies.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        device:\n          filter:\n            - integration: flare\n              model: Schedule\n    room_target:\n      name: Lights & Occupancy\n      description: >\n        Entity, device, area, floor, or label - lights within it are\n        controlled, occupancy and motion sensors within it decide when. Use\n        Exclude target to leave out sensors you don't want.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        target:\n          entity:\n            - domain: light\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: occupancy\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: motion\n            - domain: sensor\n              device_class: illuminance\n    sensors_triggers:\n      name: Sensors & Triggers\n      icon: mdi:motion-sensor\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        no_motion_wait:\n          name: Wait time\n          description: >\n            Only used when the room has occupancy or motion sensors: how long\n            every one must be clear before the room counts as empty and its\n            lights turn off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#sensors-and-triggers).\n          default: 120\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 3600\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        lux_threshold:\n          name: Lux Threshold\n          description: >\n            When every illuminance sensor in Lights & Occupancy reads above this\n            many lux, the room leaves its lights off: a sensor, a tick or a scene\n            won't switch one on until it is darker. If someone is still there\n            when it gets darker, the lights come on then. Switching the room on\n            by hand still works. 0 turns this off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#lux-threshold).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 2000\n              step: 10\n              unit_of_measurement: lx\n        extra_triggers:\n          name: Additional Triggers\n          description: >\n            Entities that make the room update as soon as they change, such as\n            an entity Scene Template or Brightness Template depends on. They\n            only adjust lights that are already on, and never switch one on.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#additional-triggers).\n          default: []\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              multiple: true\n    brightness_exclusions:\n      name: Brightness & Exclusions\n      icon: mdi:brightness-6\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        brightness_template:\n          name: Brightness Template\n          description: >\n            Template returning entity_id \u2192 brightness, 0-255, replacing\n            the curve's brightness for the lights it names (0 = off, null\n            = skip entirely). The same scale the phase brightnesses use.\n            Its own per-entity values always win over the per-phase\n            exclusions below - those only fill in entities it doesn't\n            already mention.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#brightness).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Morning\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        day_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Day\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        evening_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Evening\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        night_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Night\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n    idle_brightness:\n      name: Idle Brightness\n      icon: mdi:lightbulb-night\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        idle_brightness_template:\n          name: Idle Brightness Template\n          description: >\n            Template returning entity_id \u2192 brightness, 1-255, for\n            lights that should stay dimly lit when the room is empty,\n            instead of switching off. Its own per-entity values always\n            win over the per-phase settings below - those only fill in\n            entities it doesn't already mention.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_idle_brightness:\n          name: Morning Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        day_idle_brightness:\n          name: Day Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        evening_idle_brightness:\n          name: Evening Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        night_idle_brightness:\n          name: Night Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n    scene_handoff:\n      name: Scene Handoff\n      icon: mdi:palette-swatch\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        scene_template:\n          name: Scene Template\n          description: >\n            Template returning a scene entity_id to hand the room over\n            to instead of the adaptive brightness/colour. Takes\n            precedence over the per-phase scenes below whenever it\n            returns one - they're the fallback for phases it doesn't\n            cover.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: \"\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_scene:\n          name: Morning Scene\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        day_scene:\n          name: Day Scene\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        evening_scene:\n          name: Evening Scene\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        night_scene:\n          name: Night Scene\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    timing:\n      name: Transitions\n      icon: mdi:timer-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        motion_on_transition:\n          name: Motion On Transition\n          description: Transition duration when turning on via motion or a manual run.\n          default: 1\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        motion_off_transition:\n          name: Motion Off Transition\n          description: Transition duration when turning off via motion.\n          default: 15\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        background_transition:\n          name: Background Transition\n          description: Transition duration when the schedule, the scene template, or an Additional Trigger updates - i.e. nothing a person is actively waiting on.\n          default: 5\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n    settings:\n      name: Settings\n      icon: mdi:cog-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        override_protection:\n          name: Override Protection\n          description: >\n            Leaves a light alone once something else changes it, until all of\n            the room's lights are off. Turn it off for a room whose bulbs report\n            something other than what they show.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#override-protection).\n          default: true\n          selector:\n            boolean:\n        rgb_phases:\n          name: Prefer RGB During\n          description: >\n            Phases to send RGB colour instead of colour temperature, for\n            lights that support it (auto-detected). At the high colour\n            temperatures used during Morning/Day, this can look\n            blue-tinted rather than a clean white, so those phases are\n            off by default - Evening/Night's warmer values don't have\n            that problem.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#prefer-rgb-during).\n          default: [Evening, Night]\n          selector:\n            select:\n              options: [Morning, Day, Evening, Night]\n              multiple: true\n        stored_traces:\n          name: Stored Traces\n          description: >\n            How many of the automation's recent runs to keep traces of. The\n            room updates every minute, so this is roughly how many minutes\n            back you can look.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#stored-traces).\n          default: 20\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 1\n              max: 200\n              mode: box\n        use_area_sensors:\n          name: Sensors From Areas (Deprecated)\n          description: >\n            Deprecated and will be removed as an option in FLARE 3.0. From\n            Home Assistant 2026.11 use \"Exclude target\" instead of turning\n            this off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#sensors-from-areas).\n          default: true\n          selector:\n            boolean: {}\n\nmode: restart\nmax_exceeded: silent\ntrace:\n  stored_traces: !input stored_traces\n\n# Available to triggers and conditions, unlike variables:.\ntrigger_variables:\n  room_target: !input room_target\n  use_area_sensors: !input use_area_sensors\n  lux_threshold: !input lux_threshold\n  # The first area the room names, whose tick it follows; none if it names\n  # no area. Trigger templates can't look anything up, so only an area\n  # named directly counts.\n  tick_area: >-\n    {% set areas = room_target.area_id if room_target is mapping and room_target.area_id is defined else [] %}\n    {% set areas = [areas] if areas is string else (areas or []) %}\n    {{ areas | first if areas | length > 0 else none }}\n\ntrigger:\n  # The schedule's Phase, which fires on a real phase change (and once at\n  # startup), never on an attribute-only update.\n  - id: phase_change\n    trigger: event.received\n    target:\n      device_id: !input schedule\n    options:\n      event_type:\n        - Morning\n        - Day\n        - Evening\n        - Night\n  # The area's tick, spaced from every other area's. The curve is flat in\n  # Morning/Night, so phase_change goes quiet there. Also runs self-heal.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: event\n    event_type: flare_tick\n    event_data:\n      area_id: \"{{ tick_area }}\"\n    enabled: \"{{ tick_area is not none }}\"\n  # A room naming no area ticks on the minute instead. Every such room\n  # writes in the same second, which is what area ticks spread out.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: time_pattern\n    minutes: \"*\"\n    enabled: \"{{ tick_area is none }}\"\n  - id: extra\n    platform: state\n    entity_id: !input extra_triggers\n  # Occupancy and motion sensors share the ids. Harmless with no sensor of\n  # either kind in the room. With Sensors From Areas off, `condition:` drops\n  # those from sensors not picked by name.\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: occupancy.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: motion.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: occupancy.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: motion.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: recovered\n    platform: template\n    value_template: >\n      {#\n        Runs an ordinary tick as soon as a light becomes reachable, rather\n        than waiting for the next one. \"At least one reachable\", not \"none\n        unavailable\", so a dead entity can't block it; a bulb recovering\n        beside reachable siblings waits for the tick. Can't use `trigger.*`,\n        which isn't in scope here. Held for a few seconds, so a bulb that has\n        just powered up has booted before it's sent anything.\n      #}\n      {% set ns = namespace(entities=[], devices=[], areas=[]) %}\n      {% for key in ['entity_id', 'device_id', 'area_id', 'floor_id', 'label_id'] %}\n        {% set v = room_target.get(key, []) %}\n        {% set ids = [v] if v is string else v %}\n        {% if key == 'entity_id' %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'device_id' %}{% set ns.devices = ns.devices + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'area_id' %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'floor_id' %}\n          {% for f in ids %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + floor_areas(f) %}{% endfor %}\n        {% else %}\n          {% for l in ids %}\n            {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + label_entities(l) %}\n            {% set ns.devices = ns.devices + label_devices(l) %}\n            {% set ns.areas = ns.areas + label_areas(l) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n      {% endfor %}\n      {% for d in ns.devices %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + device_entities(d) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% for a in ns.areas %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + area_entities(a) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% set light_entity_ids = ns.entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | unique | list %}\n      {{ light_entity_ids\n         | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n         | list | length > 0 }}\n    for:\n      seconds: 5\n\n  # The room stops being too bright for Lux Threshold, so it can light up for\n  # someone already there. Only a wake-up: the action re-checks both with the\n  # room as resolve_target finds it. Expands the target the same way as\n  # `recovered`; with Sensors From Areas off, only sensors picked by name.\n  - id: lux_dark\n    platform: template\n    value_template: >\n      {% set threshold = lux_threshold | float(0) %}\n      {% set ns = namespace(entities=[], devices=[], areas=[]) %}\n      {% for key in ['entity_id', 'device_id', 'area_id', 'floor_id', 'label_id'] %}\n        {% set v = room_target.get(key, []) %}\n        {% set ids = [v] if v is string else v %}\n        {% if key == 'entity_id' %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + ids %}\n        {% elif not use_area_sensors %}\n        {% elif key == 'device_id' %}{% set ns.devices = ns.devices + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'area_id' %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'floor_id' %}\n          {% for f in ids %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + floor_areas(f) %}{% endfor %}\n        {% else %}\n          {% for l in ids %}\n            {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + label_entities(l) %}\n            {% set ns.devices = ns.devices + label_devices(l) %}\n            {% set ns.areas = ns.areas + label_areas(l) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n      {% endfor %}\n      {% for d in ns.devices %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + device_entities(d) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% for a in ns.areas %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + area_entities(a) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% set lux = ns.entities | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.')\n           | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'illuminance') | unique\n           | map('states') | select('is_number') | map('float') | list %}\n      {{ threshold > 0\n         and not (lux | length > 0 and lux | select('le', threshold) | list | count == 0) }}\n\nvariables:\n  schedule: !input schedule\n  # Who's writing, for override protection: this automation, or no one.\n  # The room's lights, released together, are resolved_entities.\n  override_protection_on: !input override_protection\n  room_id: \"{{ this.entity_id if override_protection_on else none }}\"\n  # The schedule device's one sensor, which carries the curve.\n  adaptive_sensor: >\n    {{ device_entities(schedule) | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.') | first | default(none) }}\n  scene_template: !input scene_template\n  background_transition: !input background_transition\n  motion_on_transition: !input motion_on_transition\n  no_motion_wait: !input no_motion_wait\n  lux_threshold: !input lux_threshold\n  rgb_phases: !input rgb_phases\n  phase: \"{{ states(adaptive_sensor) }}\"\n  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ phase in rgb_phases }}\"\n  script_transition: >\n    {# Slow for background updates; quick for motion or a manual run. #}\n    {% if trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id in ['phase_change', 'tick', 'extra', 'recovered', 'lux_dark'] %}\n      {{ background_transition }}\n    {% else %}\n      {{ motion_on_transition }}\n    {% endif %}\n  # Nothing triggered this run: \"Run\" was pressed, or automation.trigger\n  # was called. Forces the tick through override protection.\n  manual_run: \"{{ not (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined) }}\"\n  # Entities picked by name in Room Target, as written: the only sensors\n  # that count with Sensors From Areas off.\n  named_entities: >\n    {% set v = room_target.get('entity_id', []) %}\n    {{ [v] if v is string else v }}\n\n# Plain reading of the inputs, so it needs no resolve_target.\ncondition:\n  - alias: \"Not a sensor that Sensors From Areas leaves out\"\n    condition: template\n    value_template: >\n      {{ use_area_sensors or manual_run\n         or trigger.id not in ['motion_on', 'motion_off']\n         or trigger.entity_id in named_entities }}\n\naction:\n  # Room Target as Home Assistant resolves it for an action, which is how a\n  # flare finds its lights too. Everything below works from it, so the\n  # variables that need it are set here rather than before the trigger's\n  # conditions.\n  - alias: \"Find the room's lights and sensors\"\n    action: flare.resolve_target\n    target: !input room_target\n    response_variable: room\n  - alias: \"Work out what the room needs\"\n    variables:\n      room_entities: \"{{ room.entities }}\"\n      # Not a flare's own light, which would pass the room's values on to\n      # every light in it as an override.\n      resolved_entities: >\n        {{ room_entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | list }}\n      # The room's illuminance sensors, picked the same way as its occupancy\n      # ones: inferred from the target, or only those named with Sensors From\n      # Areas off. A sensor that isn't available or isn't numeric can't say\n      # how bright the room is, so it doesn't count.\n      room_lux_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(sensors=[]) %}\n        {% for e in room_entities | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'illuminance') %}\n          {% if states(e) | is_number %}\n            {% set ns.sensors = ns.sensors + [e] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.sensors if use_area_sensors\n           else ns.sensors | select('in', named_entities) | list }}\n      # Every illuminance sensor reading above the Lux Threshold: bright\n      # enough without the room's lights. 0 turns the check off, no sensor\n      # means nothing to go on, and a manual run (the Run button, the flare,\n      # a voice assistant) overrides it - this stops the automation lighting\n      # a bright room by itself, not someone asking for the lights.\n      too_bright: >\n        {% set threshold = lux_threshold | float(0) %}\n        {{ threshold > 0 and not manual_run\n           and room_lux_entities | length > 0\n           and room_lux_entities | map('states') | map('float', 0)\n               | select('le', threshold) | list | count == 0 }}\n      # Off lights stay off while it's too bright; ones already on are left\n      # in the call, so the curve keeps driving them.\n      lux_blocked_entities: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('is_state', 'on') | list if too_bright else [] }}\n      # Up here because variables: render top to bottom and the turn-off lists\n      # below need it.\n      template_brightness_levels: !input brightness_template\n      morning_exclude_lights: !input morning_exclude_lights\n      day_exclude_lights: !input day_exclude_lights\n      evening_exclude_lights: !input evening_exclude_lights\n      night_exclude_lights: !input night_exclude_lights\n      phase_exclude_lights: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_exclude_lights, 'Day': day_exclude_lights,\n                    'Evening': evening_exclude_lights, 'Night': night_exclude_lights} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, []) }}\n      # The template wins over the per-phase exclude list. A single number from\n      # the template means every light in the room.\n      template_brightness_map: >\n        {% set t = template_brightness_levels %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0 %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: t | float}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      brightness_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in phase_exclude_lights %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: 0}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_brightness_map) }}\n      # Lights handed off with a null/false level (\"something else owns\n      # this\"), unlike 0 (\"turn off\"). `is sameas false`, since `0 == false`\n      # in Jinja. Excluded from the turn-offs too.\n      hands_off_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for entity_id, level in brightness_levels.items() %}\n          {% if level is none or level is sameas false %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [entity_id] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      brightness: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'brightness') }}\"\n      color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'color_temp_kelvin') }}\"\n      # None while the sensor is unavailable.\n      rgb_color: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'rgb_color') }}\"\n      # Up here because the turn-off lists below exclude idle lights. Empty\n      # means dark.\n      template_idle_brightness: !input idle_brightness_template\n      morning_idle_brightness: !input morning_idle_brightness\n      day_idle_brightness: !input day_idle_brightness\n      evening_idle_brightness: !input evening_idle_brightness\n      night_idle_brightness: !input night_idle_brightness\n      phase_idle_brightness: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_idle_brightness, 'Day': day_idle_brightness,\n                    'Evening': evening_idle_brightness, 'Night': night_idle_brightness} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, 0) | int }}\n      # Same precedence as brightness_levels.\n      template_idle_map: >\n        {% set t = template_idle_brightness %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0 %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: t | float}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      idle_brightness: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% if phase_idle_brightness %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: phase_idle_brightness}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_idle_map) }}\n      # Lights that stay lit when the room empties. A null level outranks an\n      # idle one.\n      idle_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for e, level in idle_brightness.items() %}\n          {% if level and e in resolved_entities and e not in hands_off_entities\n                and e not in lux_blocked_entities %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [e] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      # Minus hands-off lights. Only feeds the motion_off turn-off.\n      reachable_entities: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | list }}\n      turn_off_entities: >\n        {{ reachable_entities | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # Every idle light has a level, so the idle calls need no brightness.\n      idle_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in idle_entities %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: idle_brightness[e]}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.m }}\n      # The room's working occupancy and motion sensors; only those picked by\n      # name with Sensors From Areas off. An unavailable or unknown sensor\n      # isn't one, so a room whose only sensor is dead counts as having none\n      # rather than as empty.\n      room_occupancy_entities: >\n        {% set sensors = (room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'occupancy') | list\n           + room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'motion') | list)\n           | reject('is_state', ['unavailable', 'unknown']) | list %}\n        {{ sensors if use_area_sensors\n           else sensors | select('in', named_entities) | list }}\n      # No occupancy sensor on, or changed, within the Wait time. Hand-written\n      # because occupancy.is_not_detected's `for:` isn't reliable after a\n      # restart. Only `on` counts as occupied, so a sensor left unavailable\n      # can't hold the room on forever. True with no sensors, so callers also\n      # check room_occupancy_entities.\n      occupancy_clear_for_wait: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(all_clear=true) %}\n        {% for e in room_occupancy_entities %}\n          {% if is_state(e, 'on') or\n                (now() - states[e].last_changed).total_seconds() < (no_motion_wait | int) %}\n            {% set ns.all_clear = false %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.all_clear }}\n      # Empty, with lights that stay dimly lit. Suppresses the curve while\n      # idle: an idle light being on makes `occupied`, and so allow_turn_on,\n      # true, which would ramp the nightlight straight back up.\n      room_is_idle: >\n        {{ idle_entities | length > 0\n           and room_occupancy_entities | length > 0\n           and occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\n      occupied: >\n        {# The room is in use if anything it runs is already on. #}\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('in', hands_off_entities)\n           | select('is_state', 'on') | list | count > 0 }}\n      # THE gate for switching a light on: motion, a manual run, the room\n      # already in use, or the room getting dark enough while someone is in it\n      # (Lux Threshold, at the user's request). Only two things may switch a\n      # light on:\n      #\n      #   scene.turn_on / flare.apply_lighting - inside default:'s single\n      #     `if allow_turn_on` block.\n      #   flare.apply_lighting for idle brightness - gated on idle_entities and\n      #     occupancy_clear_for_wait instead.\n      #\n      # Lux Threshold narrows both: too_bright drops the off lights from each\n      # call and keeps the scene from activating.\n      #\n      # Anything new that can switch a light on needs one of those gates. The\n      # idle gate must stay narrower than allow_turn_on, and must not be gated\n      # on `occupied`, which an idle light makes true.\n      allow_turn_on: >\n        {{ manual_run\n           or (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id == 'motion_on')\n           or occupied\n           or (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id == 'lux_dark'\n               and not too_bright\n               and room_occupancy_entities | length > 0 and not occupancy_clear_for_wait) }}\n      # Retried by self-heal. Excludes hands-off and idle lights.\n      entities_still_on: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | select('is_state', 'on')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # The room's entities and every entity on each light's device, for\n      # scene-compatibility checks.\n      scope_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(entities=room_entities) %}\n        {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n          {% set did = device_id(e) %}\n          {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + (device_entities(did) if did else [e]) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.entities | unique | list }}\n      morning_scene: !input morning_scene\n      day_scene: !input day_scene\n      evening_scene: !input evening_scene\n      night_scene: !input night_scene\n      phase_scene: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_scene, 'Day': day_scene, 'Evening': evening_scene, 'Night': night_scene} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase) }}\n      # scene_template wins when it returns a valid scene; a typo or missing\n      # scene counts as nothing. The entity_id shape check has to come first:\n      # states[] raises on a malformed string, aborting the whole run.\n      desired_scene: >\n        {% set candidate = (scene_template | trim) %}\n        {% if candidate and candidate is match('^[a-z0-9_]+\\\\.[a-z0-9_]+$') and states[candidate] is not none %}\n          {{ candidate }}\n        {% elif phase_scene and states[phase_scene] is not none %}\n          {{ phase_scene }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ '' }}\n        {% endif %}\n      # Re-activating a scene every minute would stomp manual changes, so the\n      # tick never does.\n      scene_recheck_due: \"{{ not (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id == 'tick') }}\"\n      # No scene until flare.compute_scene_coverage says otherwise, in default:.\n      scene_coverage: \"{{ {'scene_valid': false, 'covered_entities': []} }}\"\n  # Never checks occupancy: an already-on light should follow the curve\n  # regardless. allow_turn_on decides whether lights may come on.\n  #\n  # motion_on stops if there's nothing to do - nothing off and nothing\n  # idle. `idle_entities`, not `room_is_idle`, which is false once motion\n  # starts.\n  - alias: \"Stop a motion_on run with nothing to turn on\"\n    if:\n      - condition: trigger\n        alias: \"Triggered by motion_on\"\n        id: motion_on\n      - condition: template\n        alias: \"Nothing in the room is off, and nothing has an idle level\"\n        value_template: >-\n          {{ resolved_entities | map('states') | select('ne', 'on') | list | count == 0\n             and idle_entities | length == 0 }}\n    then:\n      - stop: \"Nothing to turn on\"\n  - choose:\n      # The cleared triggers' `for:` is per sensor, so they fire once each\n      # sensor's own Wait time is up, even if another saw motion since.\n      - alias: \"Motion timed out and the room is confirmed empty\"\n        conditions:\n          - condition: trigger\n            alias: \"Triggered by motion_off\"\n            id: motion_off\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Every occupancy sensor has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n        sequence:\n          # flare.turn_off keeps them FLARE's, so they aren't read as overridden\n          # while idle lights keep the room lit.\n          - alias: \"Turn off the light(s)\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ turn_off_entities }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n          # Idle lights are dimmed instead. Does nothing with no idle brightness.\n          - alias: \"Leave the idle-brightness lights dimly lit\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Room has idle-brightness lights to dim\"\n                value_template: \"{{ idle_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n            then:\n              - action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: !input motion_off_transition\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n                  room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n      # Self-heal: on a tick, with the room empty, retry turn-offs that didn't\n      # land. Exclusive of default:, which would work from the same stale list.\n      - alias: \"Self-heal: retry an earlier turn-off that didn't land\"\n        conditions:\n          # phase_change too: moving to a phase with no idle brightness leaves\n          # lights on that no longer read as idle.\n          - condition: trigger\n            alias: \"Triggered by the periodic tick or a phase change\"\n            id:\n              - tick\n              - phase_change\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room has an occupancy sensor to reconcile against\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_occupancy_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n          # Continuously clear for the full Wait time, so a sensor blip can't turn\n          # lights off.\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Occupancy has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Something in the room is still on\"\n            value_template: \"{{ entities_still_on | length > 0 }}\"\n        sequence:\n          - alias: \"Self-heal: retry turning off lights left on with no occupancy\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ entities_still_on }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n    default:\n      - alias: \"Work out which lights the scene takes, if there is one\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"A scene is chosen\"\n            value_template: \"{{ desired_scene | length > 0 }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Compute scene coverage (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.compute_scene_coverage\n            data:\n              scene_entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n              scope_entities: \"{{ scope_entities }}\"\n              target_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n            response_variable: scene_coverage\n      # The scene counts only if it exists and everything it covers is in\n      # scope; otherwise FLARE drives every light.\n      - variables:\n          scene_valid: \"{{ scene_coverage.scene_valid }}\"\n          # Lights handed off this run - to an active scene, or via a\n          # null/false level. They're never written, so their claims are\n          # released instead of going stale into \"overridden\". Lights only: a\n          # scene can set other domains, which hold no claims.\n          handed_off_entities: >\n            {{ ((scene_coverage.covered_entities if scene_valid else []) + hands_off_entities)\n               | select('match', 'light[.]') | unique | list }}\n          # No off-light filter: the step using it is already behind\n          # allow_turn_on. Off lights are dropped while the room is too\n          # bright, so the call updates the ones already on and leaves the\n          # rest dark.\n          target_entities: >\n            {{ (scene_coverage.uncovered_entities if scene_valid else resolved_entities)\n               | reject('in', lux_blocked_entities) | list }}\n      # Everything that can switch a light on is under this gate (see\n      # allow_turn_on). An empty room settles to its idle brightness, outside\n      # the gate. room_occupancy_entities is checked because a room with no\n      # sensors would otherwise always read as empty.\n      - alias: \"Settle an empty room to its idle brightness\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room is idle, and the sensor has a colour target\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_is_idle and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Apply idle brightness (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.apply_lighting\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n              brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n              color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n              rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n              transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n              prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n              room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n              room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n      - alias: \"Only motion, a manual run, or a room already in use may switch a light on\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Allowed to turn on, and not already handled by the idle nightlight\"\n            # Stops the nightlight ramping itself back up (see room_is_idle).\n            value_template: \"{{ allow_turn_on and not room_is_idle }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Activate a scene, if one applies and is due a recheck\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"A scene applies and is due a recheck, and can't light a bright room\"\n                # Activating it sets every light it covers, so while it's too\n                # bright only once they're all on already. Its lights stay the\n                # scene's either way.\n                value_template: >\n                  {{ scene_valid and scene_recheck_due\n                     and (not too_bright\n                          or scene_coverage.covered_entities | select('match', 'light[.]')\n                             | reject('is_state', 'on') | list | count == 0) }}\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Activate matching scene\"\n                action: scene.turn_on\n                target:\n                  entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n                data:\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n          # Guarded because the sensor attributes render null when the sensor is\n          # unavailable, and apply_lighting requires both.\n          - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting, unless the sensor has no target to apply\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Sensor has a real brightness and colour target\"\n                value_template: \"{{ brightness is not none and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting (FLARE)\"\n                action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ target_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ brightness_levels }}\"\n                  brightness: \"{{ brightness }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n                  room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n                  # A manual run forces the tick through override protection.\n                  force: \"{{ manual_run }}\"\n      # Bookkeeping only, so outside the gate.\n      - alias: \"Release lights handed off to a scene or another owner\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"There are lights to release, with override protection on\"\n            value_template: >-\n              {{ room_id is not none and handed_off_entities | length > 0 }}\n        then:\n          - action: flare.claims_clear\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ handed_off_entities }}\"\n", "tree": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 1, "__end_line__": 962, "value": {"blueprint": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 2, "__end_line__": 338, "value": {"name": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 2, "__end_line__": 2, "value": "FLARE"}, "description": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 3, "__end_line__": 12, "value": "FLARE: phase-based circadian lighting - sets brightness/colour temperature from a FLARE schedule sensor, keeping lights updated as it changes, and turns them off a while after occupancy clears. Full details on every input: [the blueprint reference](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/).\n\nBlueprint version 0.0.0-dev - the integration raises a repair when a newer one is available.\n"}, "domain": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 13, "__end_line__": 13, "value": "automation"}, "author": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 14, "__end_line__": 14, "value": "Dan Spencer"}, "homeassistant": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 17, "__end_line__": 18, "value": {"min_version": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 17, "__end_line__": 17, "value": "2026.4.0"}}}, "input": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 19, "__end_line__": 338, "value": {"schedule": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 20, "__end_line__": 30, "value": {"name": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 20, "__end_line__": 20, "value": "Schedule"}, "description": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 21, "__end_line__": 24, "value": "The FLARE schedule the room follows: the brightness and colour temperature it applies. [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n"}, "selector": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 26, "__end_line__": 30, "value": {"device": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 27, "__end_line__": 30, "value": {"filter": {"__type__": "seq", "__line__": 28, "__end_line__": 30, "value": [{"__type__": "map", "__line__": 28, "__end_line__": 30, "value": {"integration": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 28, "__end_line__": 28, "value": "flare"}, "model": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 29, "__end_line__": 29, "value": "Schedule"}}}]}}}}}}}, "room_target": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 31, "__end_line__": 47, "value": {"name": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 31, "__end_line__": 31, "value": "Lights & Occupancy"}, "description": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 32, "__end_line__": 36, "value": "Entity, device, area, floor, or label - lights within it are c